{"id":"q35","run":1,"role":"calibration","category":"math","question":"Is 2^20 + 1 a prime number?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":null,"claims":[{"text":"2^20 + 1 = 1,048,577 is composite.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Numbers of the form 2^k + 1 can be prime only when k is a power of 2.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Since 20 is not a power of 2, the Fermat pattern suggests compositeness but does not prove it.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"There is no other obvious structural reason to expect 2^20 + 1 to be prime.","confidence":0.8,"lean":-1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Because 20 has an odd factor greater than 1 (5), the expression factors.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"2^20 + 1 = 16^5 + 1, and a^n + 1 is divisible by a + 1 when n is odd, so 17 divides it.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"1,048,577 = 17 × 61,681, so 17 is a nontrivial divisor.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The explicit factorization 17 × 61,681 proves the number is not prime, while the Fermat heuristic only suggested it.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.95,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":4,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"